# Relates to

Fixes #31049. Supersedes #31416 with the same reviewed plugin source rebased onto develop `8a94d74acc`, and production evaluator/HTTP/PGlite acceptance.

# Background

Registered custom form types previously did not govern top-level parsing, validation, formatting, or extraction prompts. This change uses the per-runtime type at each boundary, preserves explicit legacy handler precedence over built-ins, and masks sensitive values before custom formatting. Calendar answers normalize to validated YYYY-MM-DD days without a timezone shift; strict number parsing remains intact.

# Risks and documentation

Date fields reject impossible, yearless, and timestamp-shaped inputs instead of inventing a calendar day. Existing timestamp-shaped persisted values are not migrated. This implements the documented registration contract; no routes or UI change.

# Sync and testing

- Rebased onto develop `8a94d74acc`; clean working tree.
- Frozen normal install passed, with documented ELIZA_SKIP_FUSED_INFERENCE_SETUP=1. Native inference is outside this change.
- 155 package tests passed across 11 files.
- Root `bun run verify`: exit 0; 373/373 tasks passed, 142 cached, 6m40.605s task duration; all repository audits passed (11,912 test files scanned, zero focused tests or orphaned skips).
- Actual FormService and EvaluatorService, actual plugin-openai SDK/HTTP transport, actual SQL/PGlite migrations, persisted readback, and clean runtime shutdown passed with two known-value responses.

